ived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zib4ik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zib4ik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zib4ik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zib4ik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ShlomiZevin/aspect-agent-client-react/commits/b432dcfcb181acd38b9acac3f47d4c2127f31c73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T08:20:17Z","email":"ziben.konstantin@gmail.com","name":"Ziben Konstantin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T08:20:17Z","email":"ziben.konstantin@gmail.com","name":"Ziben Konstantin"},"message":"Intelligence: show a clean error, not the raw server message (task #85)\n\nJobSidebar''s error box rendered job.errorMessage verbatim - the\nserver''s internal English debugging prose (\"The data needed to answer\nthis isn''t available in this dataset - the query for ... returned no\nrows.\", a timeout stack, etc.) landing directly in the UI, unlocalized,\neven under the Hebrew toggle. This is what Shlomi flagged across\n\"all Intelligence Centers\" - the component is shared by every dataset,\nso the bug wasn''t dataset-specific.\n\nNow shows the existing bilingual generic message\n(intel.sidebar.errorDefault) instead; the raw text moves to the box''s\ntitle attribute as a hover tooltip, the same pattern JobBadge already\nuses for its own failed-badge label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"98d852b0530f71eb43471e091cb60c4295453f36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ShlomiZevin/aspect-agent-client-react/git/trees/98d852b0530f71eb43471e091cb60c4295453f36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ShlomiZevin/aspect-agent-client-react/git/commits/b432dcfcb181acd38b9acac3f47d4c2127f31c73","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatar