/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zib4ik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zib4ik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ShlomiZevin/aspect-agent-client-react/commits/2d6933a389402dfb556422c7757d3c365f33ebd3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T07:56:02Z","email":"ziben.konstantin@gmail.com","name":"Ziben Konstantin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T07:56:02Z","email":"ziben.konstantin@gmail.com","name":"Ziben Konstantin"},"message":"Dashboard: Modules tab for the aspect agent points at the right dataset\n\nOtto was enabled and ready under the aspect Intelligence dataset (task,\n2026-09-16) but Shlomi couldn''t see it on the aspect dashboard\n(WhatsApp, 2026-09-17). Cause: the Modules route was wired to\nconfig.database?.schema, which for the aspect agent''s CHAT is zer4u -\na real but separate dataset from the aspect Intelligence dataset\n(registry.js''s synthetic TechZone demo, task #73). Every other agent\nhas schema === slug === Intelligence dataset id, so this never showed\nelsewhere; aspect is the one agent where chat and Intelligence\ngenuinely point at different datasets.\n\nSpecial-cased the Modules tab specifically (not Data Loader / Query\nOptimizer, which correctly still need zer4u for the aspect agent''s\nchat) to use the literal ''aspect'' dataset id, matching the Intelligence\nside the module is actually registered under.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a90ded40bc992c07f79305bd1cd1d10889e748b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ShlomiZevin/aspect-agent-client-react/git/trees/a90ded40bc992c07f79305bd1cd1d10889e748b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ShlomiZevin/aspect-agent-client-react/git/commits/2d6933a389402dfb556422c7757d3c365f33ebd3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://a